<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador bank liquidity down 2.38 pct by Jan 1.</title>
<headline>Ecuador bank liquidity down 2.38 pct by Jan 1.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's Central Bank said Monday liquidity in the banking system fell 2.38 percent, or 411 million sucres, to 16.85 billion sucres in the week to January 10.</p>
<p>Total liquidity in the banking sector ended 1996 at 16.99 billion sucres, up 35.8 percent from 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
</text>
